# Documentation

## Split

| Doc | Contains |
|-----|----------|
| `docs/PRD.md` | Product behavior, backlog, non-goals, constraints |
| `README.md` | Quick start, deploy, `config.js` format, stop-ID lookup |
| `AGENTS.md` | Short index linking PRD + rules |

## Rules

- Do not duplicate API URL blocks in both PRD and README — link instead
- User-visible behavior changes → update `docs/PRD.md`
- Setup/deploy/config changes → update `README.md`
- When README describes app behavior, verify against `js/config.js` and `js/app.js`

## Ship checklist (agent — do automatically)

When completing work, follow [workflow.mdc](workflow.mdc). In the same turn as code:

1. `docs/PRD.md` — backlog → Current behavior; constraints if needed
2. `README.md` — only if setup or "How it works" summary is wrong
3. Matching rule file (`javascript.mdc`, `styles.mdc`, `product.mdc`, or `docs.mdc`)

Do not mark a task complete without these updates.

## Drift checks

README must reflect current `REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS` and major features listed in PRD "Current behavior". If unsure, PRD is the behavior source of truth.
